 "note": "Parameter renames between ArduCopter 4.6.3 and 4.7.1, for ap-upgrade-verify.py --renames. factor converts an old value to the new scale: new = old * factor. Factors are read off the 4.7.1 source conversion code, not the metadata units field, which does not record every scale change (PSC_ACCZ_P/I/D, PSC_ACCZ_IMAX and PSC_VELZ_IMAX scale by 0.1, 0.001 and 0.01 with no unit change). The how field of each row says how it was established: a conversion table (file and line), a conversion in place, or a rename in place. Three rows were not checked and say so. A rename in place keeps its storage slot, so its factor is 1. unit_old and unit_new are the metadata units at each version, for reading only. The 4.7.1 description of PSC_D_ACC_FF says it is PSC_ACCZ_FF * 0.1, but its conversion table copies it unscaled; this map follows the table.",
